A||N||4||ikarian||starts and idles fine, but stalls when put in gear||||5||
Z||000000||ikarian||03-09-2001||12:54 AM||||I have recently run into a problem with my '84 Fiero (4-cyl coupe).  I can start my car and it idles perfectly - but when I put it in gear, it stalls.  At times, I can get it in gear, but as soon as I give it gas, I can hear it missing as if it was running on three cylinders then dies.  <P>I replaced EGR valve, spark plugs and wires.  I also checked to make sure I don't have any vaccuum leaks.<P>Any input would be appreciated.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||03-09-2001||06:27 AM||||If it's an auto try disconnecting the TCC wire (side of tranny). If the problem goes away replace the unit.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever2||03-10-2001||02:59 AM||||Bringing this back to the top for ya.  Yer welcome.  And a big PFF "howdy"!<P>Hope to see you at the club meeting.  I told the club Prez you're coming and he made reservations, so now you HAVE to be there!  Another new guy I invited is coming, so you won't be in the spotlight by yourself. Perfect time to slip in unnoticed if you're shy about that kind of thing.<P>Okay, now, did you make any progress on that stalling problem?<P>BTW, go ahead and put your website on your profile.  I forgot to write it down last night, sorry.<P>------------------<BR><I>Chuck Hodges</I><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 03-10-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000003||theogre||03-10-2001||11:48 AM||||check MAP, it's vacuum line for damage/blockage, and timing.||||reg||1
Z||000004||ikarian||03-10-2001||04:53 PM||||Problem solved!!  Thank you for the input.  Before I messed with the TCC or MAP sensor, I replaced the distributor cap and rotor (hadn't done that in years).  It's running great (240,000 miles and going strong - not bad for a 4 banger).  In fact, I'm going to drive it to the Houston Fiero meeting this afternoon.||||reg||10
